KG42.register("rules-5b72f641a8704c90d6a3f75f",{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R010","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"P2P transactions carry a transaction cost that includes a network tariff for using physical grid facilities and an aggregator service fee. Scope: P2P energy transactions in the proposed local market with residential shared energy storage.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["settlement.payment"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"P2P energy transactions in the proposed local market with residential shared energy storage.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R010-X001","symbol":"p^{t}_{sb}","meaning":"P2P transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t, on which the P2P transaction cost is levied.","kind":"operational","domain":"p^{t}_{sb} \\ge 0 (source nonnegativity condition)","unit":null,"indices":["s","b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-T001","symbol":"\\lambda^{t}_{cost}","meaning":"P2P transaction cost in period t, including the network tariff for using physical grid facilities and the aggregator service fee.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-T002","symbol":"\\Delta t","meaning":"Duration of a period.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E21"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"P2P transactions carry a transaction cost that includes a network tariff for using physical grid facilities and an aggregator service fee. Scope: P2P energy transactions in the proposed local market with residential shared energy storage.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For each seller s and period t, the P2P transaction-cost term in the seller's profit is the per-unit P2P transaction cost λ^{t}_{cost} times the sum of the seller's P2P transaction amounts over buyers, multiplied by the period duration Δt.","expression":"\\lambda^{t}_{cost}\\left(\\sum_{b\\in B}p^{t}_{sb}\\right)\\Delta t,\\quad \\forall s\\in S,\\ t\\in T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R010-T001","v141-c-R010-T002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"gy , pi to decision-making problem can be cast as ∑ ∑ ∑ ∑ e. max : ( ρtsbptsb + λtsell(Pts − ptsb) −","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where p^{t}_{sb} and \\rho^{t}_{sb} are decision variables. p^{t}_{sb} is the transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t. \\rho^{t}_{sb} is transaction price associated with p^{t}_{sb}. However, the market-clearing price \\rho^{t}_{sb} is out of control of seller s and buyer b but is determined by the market equilibrium problem of the game. Parameter P^{t}_{s} is the renewable energy for sale of seller s in period t. Parameter \\lambda^{t}_{sell} is FiT when a seller sells its energy to the power grid. Parameter \\lambda^{t}_{cost} is the P2P transaction cost, including network tariff for using the physical grid facilities and aggregator service fee."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"he ergy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling an energy to the power g","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"The objective of each energy seller is to maximize its profit. In the objective function (1), the first term is the revenue of trading with energy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling energy to the power grid in the FiT scheme. After participating in the P2P transaction, energy seller can still sell their surplus to the power grid to get more income. The third term is the transaction cost for P2P transactions. Constraint (2) stipulates that total P2P transaction amounts in period t should not exceed the seller’s initial excessive energy. Constraint (3) is for the non-negativity condition for the decision variable p^{t}_{sb}. \\upsilon^{t}_{s} and \\omega^{t}_{sb} after the colon are dual variables of the constraints."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 308 (2022) 118400 of energy sellers, energy buyers, and market equilibrium are presen","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In our model, the P2P market consists of energy buyers and sellers. Let S denote the set of energy sellers, with the typical energy seller s ∈ S. Let B denote the set of energy buyers, with the typical energy seller b ∈ B. The operational problem is solved during multi-periods and T is the set of all periods. t ∈ T is a typical single period with an equal duration of Δt."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 308 (2022) 118400 of energy sellers, energy buyers, and market equilibrium are presen","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For each rational energy seller s ∈ S, it maximizes its profit and the decision-making problem can be cast as\nmax : \\sum_{t\\in T}\\left(\\sum_{b\\in B}\\rho^{t}_{sb}p^{t}_{sb}+\\lambda^{t}_{sell}\\left(P^{t}_{s}-\\sum_{b\\in B}p^{t}_{sb}\\right)-\\lambda^{t}_{cost}\\sum_{b\\in B}p^{t}_{sb}\\right)\\Delta t \\quad (1)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"gy , pi to decision-making problem can be cast as ∑ ∑ ∑ ∑ e. max : ( ρtsbptsb + λtsell(Pts − ptsb) −","equation_id":"(2)-(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"s.t. \\sum_{b\\in B}p^{t}_{sb}\\leqslant P^{t}_{s} : \\upsilon^{t}_{s}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (2)\np^{t}_{sb}\\geqslant 0 : \\omega^{t}_{sb}, \\forall b\\in B, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p02-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"Indices and sets V B Set of energy buyers pts S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers ρ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Indices and sets B Set of energy buyers S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers s The index of energy sellers T Set of time periods t Index of time periods Parameters \\Delta t Duration of period \\lambda^{t}_{sell} Feed-in Tariff in period t \\lambda^{t}_{cost} P2P transaction cost in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy} The TLOU price of energy buyer b in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy0} Initial electricity price in TLOU in period t k^{t} Constant coefficient in TLOU P^{t}_{s} The energy supply of seller s in period t D^{t}_{b} The energy demand of buyer b in period t \\eta_{c} Charging efficiency \\eta_{d} Discharging efficiency p^{u} Maximal charging/discharging power Q^{0}_{b} Initial energy storage level of buyer b Q_{m} Capacity of the shared energy storage units Variables p^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t \\rho^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction price between seller s and buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bg} Energy from the grid of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bc} Charging power of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bd} Discharging power of buyer b in period t Q_{b} Capacity allocation of buyer b Q^{t}_{b} Energy storage level of buyer b in period t"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E13","quote":"the P2P transaction cost, including network tariff for using the physical grid facilities and aggregator service fee."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","quote":"The third term is the transaction cost for P2P transactions."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"5d209e403d65f168c2cca7a1ef6d35691d8d379d9e736d1f7992846259156007","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The source explicitly defines the P2P transaction cost as including a network tariff and aggregator service fee and gives its aggregate term in the seller's objective. The formalization captures the aggregate seller-side P2P transaction-cost term; the source does not assign separate symbols to the network-tariff and aggregator-fee components, so they are not decomposed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-X001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The P2P transaction amount p^{t}_{sb} is the quantity on which the settlement.payment transaction cost is levied; the source defines it in the seller problem and relates it to the P2P transaction cost."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-T001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"λ^{t}_{cost} is the source-defined P2P transaction cost parameter used in settlement.payment, including the network tariff and aggregator service fee."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-T002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Δt is the period-duration parameter that scales the P2P transaction-cost term in the source seller objective."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The formalized seller-side P2P transaction-cost term belongs to the settlement.payment node; no graph edge is needed for this unary cost relation."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
